      "message": "No, In the computeInitialDelay method we perform the modulo operation so the delay will always be (-interval, interval), however if delay is  \u003c\u003d 0, we add interval to it so if jitter is present, delay will always be (jitter, interval + jitter].\n\n```\nlong delay \u003d Duration.between(now, startTime).toMillis() % interval;\nif (delay \u003c\u003d 0) {\n   delay +\u003d interval;\n}\n```",
